export tt_020125() =>
    "
     👉  Czech National Bank Considers Bitcoin Reserves [Financial Times]:\n\n
     ▢  The Czech National Bank, under Governor Aleš Michl, is exploring the possibility of allocating up to 5% of its €140 billion reserves into Bitcoin to diversify its assets.\n
     ▢  If approved, this move would make it the first Western central bank to hold cryptocurrency as a reserve asset.\n
     ▢  Impact on Crypto: Such a decision could legitimize Bitcoin as a reserve asset, potentially leading to increased adoption by other central banks and influencing Bitcoin's market value.\n\n\n
     👉  Federal Reserve's Stance on Holding Bitcoin [Reuters]:\n\n
     ▢  Federal Reserve Chair Jerome Powell stated in December 2024 that the Fed is legally prohibited from owning Bitcoin and has no intention of seeking a change to that regulation.\n
     ▢  This position indicates potential challenges for integrating Bitcoin into federal monetary frameworks.\n
     ▢  Impact on Crypto: The Fed's reluctance may temper market enthusiasm, potentially leading to short-term volatility in Bitcoin's price.\n\n\n
     👉  Global Interest in Bitcoin as a Reserve Asset [Forbes]:\n\n
     ▢  Beyond the US, countries like El Salvador and Bhutan have begun incorporating Bitcoin into their national reserves.\n
     ▢  This trend reflects a growing global acceptance of Bitcoin as a strategic asset.\n
     ▢  Impact on Crypto: Increased adoption by nation-states could enhance Bitcoin's credibility and contribute to its long-term appreciation."

export tt_070125() =>
